WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:06.764
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:07.264 --> 00:00:08.065
Dammit.

00:00:08.065 --> 00:00:10.801
How come that catwalk
doesn't have any supports?

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:14.004
The last one had dangling
cables after it collapsed.

00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:18.108
If I had one of those, I could 
swing
across to the other side like 
Tarzan.

00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:19.610
That would be dope.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.645
They did that in Star Wars, too.

00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:25.015
Dude swinging across a gap with
some babe holding onto him.

00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:26.784
That was a grappling hook, 
though.

00:00:27.284 --> 00:00:30.087
That's what this suit needs:
a grappling hook.

00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:34.391
Then I could swing my way to 
victory
instead of performing this 
balancing act.

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:38.729
Bugs can crawl on walls. 
Maybe I should've been a bug.

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:40.664
Go Team Kafka!

00:00:40.664 --> 00:00:43.700
I'd at least want four arms
like the god Shiva.

00:00:44.268 --> 00:00:46.270
Okay, now I have some options.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.906
I can either fall to my
death in this black pit,

00:00:48.906 --> 00:00:52.476
land on the edge and gore myself
on the jagged metal mesh,

00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:55.212
or land on the concrete and
maybe break my legs.

00:00:55.212 --> 00:00:58.382
And before, all I had was the 
pit.

00:00:58.382 --> 00:01:00.017
Jee-heez!

00:01:00.017 --> 00:01:03.754
I'm going to have arthritis by
the time I'm 30 at this rate.

00:01:03.754 --> 00:01:06.657
Assuming I even live that long.

00:01:06.657 --> 00:01:08.025
Ah, who am I kidding?

00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:09.793
I've got a gun.

00:01:09.793 --> 00:01:12.963
Oh, what the hell?
Another catwalk is out?

00:01:12.963 --> 00:01:14.765
And what is THAT?

00:01:14.765 --> 00:01:17.234
It's got tentacles for a face.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.836
It's a Cthulhu dog.

00:01:19.503 --> 00:01:22.606
Well, it's attacking the 
face-huggers;
it can't be all bad.

00:01:22.606 --> 00:01:24.608
I'll just wait until it's
done with them and--

00:01:24.608 --> 00:01:28.345
[coughing]

00:01:28.345 --> 00:01:31.415
Plegh!  Tastes like
dead caterpillars!  Pleh!

00:01:31.415 --> 00:01:32.916
Okay, squid-head.

00:01:34.685 --> 00:01:38.655
Say hello to Yog-Sothoth
and the Elder Gods for me!

00:01:39.723 --> 00:01:40.524
Hey, a rope!

00:01:40.524 --> 00:01:41.959
Now I can be Tarzan!

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:44.061
[Tarzan yell]

00:01:44.061 --> 00:01:45.629
Hey, wait, that's not a rope.

00:01:45.629 --> 00:01:48.966
That's a...these are like...
jellyfish or something.

00:01:48.966 --> 00:01:51.635
If I swung on that, it could
come crashing down on me.

00:01:51.635 --> 00:01:54.304
These aliens are just good for 
nothing.

00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:58.442
These crates are good for 
something.

00:01:58.442 --> 00:02:00.143
This one just broke my fall.

00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:03.280
That means aliens are
worth less than crates.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.082
Which is, what, a few bucks?

00:02:08.085 --> 00:02:10.287
Well, at least I got to rinse my
mouth out.

00:02:10.287 --> 00:02:12.089
What I really need is some 
toothpaste,

00:02:12.089 --> 00:02:15.125
but now it tastes a little
bit less like squid snot.

00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:18.729
If that water's toxic, too, then
at
least the toxins are tasteless.

00:02:18.729 --> 00:02:21.198
I'll have time to worry about
mouth cancer later.

00:02:21.665 --> 00:02:22.332
Hey, wait.

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:24.534
What's up with this ceiling?

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:30.007
That looks like a ceiling 
designed to
have moving walls that crush 
people.

00:02:30.007 --> 00:02:31.508
Well, there's no bloodstains.

00:02:31.942 --> 00:02:34.144
Oh, God.  That was a pun.

00:02:34.144 --> 00:02:36.313
"What's up with this ceiling?"

00:02:36.313 --> 00:02:37.581
What's wrong with me?

00:02:37.581 --> 00:02:40.450
I'd punch somebody in the
mouth if they said that to me.

00:02:40.784 --> 00:02:42.653
Huh.  Wow....

00:02:42.653 --> 00:02:44.588
I wasn't expecting this.

00:02:44.588 --> 00:02:47.791
This... this must be our
box-smashing room.

00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.227
I mean, what, we have a 
bottomless pit,

00:02:50.227 --> 00:02:54.965
and the sides are all plate 
metal that look
strong enough to withstand a 
missile blast.

00:02:54.965 --> 00:02:58.235
This room must've cost a couple
hundred thousand to build.

00:02:58.235 --> 00:03:00.504
Eat your heart out, taxpayers.

00:03:00.504 --> 00:03:02.439
This is where your money goes.

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:05.609
I mean, we get most of our money
from the Department of Defense,

00:03:05.609 --> 00:03:07.811
and this is what
we're spending it on.

00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:10.614
And here, I thought my
division was wasting money.

00:03:10.614 --> 00:03:13.550
We were doing a hell of a lot
more than smashing boxes.

00:03:14.184 --> 00:03:16.620
This whole company's just 
retarded.

00:03:17.354 --> 00:03:20.424
Ugh, there's no door up here.

00:03:20.424 --> 00:03:23.060
Is there really no way around 
this?

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.461
What do the workers normally do?

00:03:24.461 --> 00:03:27.331
Just ride the crates down
like it's a ski-lift?

00:03:28.265 --> 00:03:29.066
Well...

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:33.170
Okay, extreme hopscotch!

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.104
Let's do this!

00:03:35.539 --> 00:03:37.474
No room for error here.

00:03:37.474 --> 00:03:41.378
It kind of reminds me of that 
cooking
show I saw filmed in the 
Philippines,

00:03:41.378 --> 00:03:45.082
where two chefs would compete 
against
each other to make the best 
dish,

00:03:45.082 --> 00:03:48.952
and, at the end, they would cut
the loser's head off with a 
sword.

00:03:48.952 --> 00:03:50.554
I think the show got cancelled.

00:03:52.122 --> 00:03:56.560
Well, now I have an answer if 
anyone ever
asks me what the dumbest thing 
I've ever did was.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.461
I can say-WHOA!

00:03:58.128 --> 00:04:01.398
"There was this one time I was 
jumping
across these crates suspended 
above

00:04:01.398 --> 00:04:04.501
"a bottomless pit, even though
I didn't really know where I was
going.

00:04:05.302 --> 00:04:08.038
"Or-or-or, there was the time
I crawled into a drainage pipe,

00:04:08.038 --> 00:04:10.207
"opened up the floodgate
and almost drowned.

00:04:10.207 --> 00:04:11.808
"I shouldn't even be alive, 
really."

00:04:12.776 --> 00:04:13.844
Ahh, made it.

00:04:14.511 --> 00:04:17.581
So, where do these things go
that we need so many crates?

00:04:18.782 --> 00:04:20.350
That doesn't go anywhere.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.284
That's a wall.

00:04:22.152 --> 00:04:23.420
That....

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.523
That means we're just loading up
crates
so we can drop them over that 
pit.

00:04:27.224 --> 00:04:31.061
That means that there's no
damned point to this whole room.

00:04:31.061 --> 00:04:33.397
This whole place is such a wash.

00:04:33.397 --> 00:04:36.900
Good ol' New Mexico.  We're 
really
making a name for the state.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.703
First, they invented the
atomic bomb in Los Alamos.

00:04:39.703 --> 00:04:43.407
Now, we've invented mean-ass 
aliens
that teleport out of nowhere.

00:04:43.407 --> 00:04:45.342
I'm not sure which is worse.

00:04:45.342 --> 00:04:47.411
You know, when they
invented the atomic bomb,

00:04:47.411 --> 00:04:50.080
they were afraid it was going to
catch the atmosphere on fire

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.983
and burn up the whole earth, but
they did it anyway.

00:04:52.983 --> 00:04:54.518
That took balls.

00:04:54.518 --> 00:04:55.719
Not us, though.

00:04:55.719 --> 00:04:57.254
The only people taking the risks

00:04:57.254 --> 00:05:00.023
were the ones that didn't
understand them in the first 
place.

00:05:00.023 --> 00:05:01.258
We're not brave.

00:05:01.258 --> 00:05:02.692
We're just stupid.

00:05:03.927 --> 00:05:05.629
Well, I'm on the other side.

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:07.664
So, that's what?
Three-for-three?

00:05:07.664 --> 00:05:11.168
Man, we've picked the wrong
contractor to build these 
catwalks.

00:05:11.168 --> 00:05:13.470
El Sleazo's Discount 
Construction.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.339
Bribing building inspectors for
over 40 years.

00:05:17.641 --> 00:05:18.642
YES!

00:05:18.642 --> 00:05:21.144
Time to get the hell out of 
here.

00:05:24.648 --> 00:05:26.648
I hate elevator music.

